      "caption": "Judge training paradigms positioned by training cost and bias-mitigation strength. Both axes are ordinal rankings argued in this appendix, not measured quantities. Marker shape encodes the supervision source. The dashed guide marks the direction the field has moved, away from expensive teacher-dependent training toward paradigms that reach comparable bias resistance for less, with representation probing at the extreme. RL with verifiable rewards is the exception on cost: it buys the strongest bias mitigation at the highest training expense.",
