      "panel": null,
      "label": "fig:paradigm_supervision",
      "parentLabel": "fig:paradigm_supervision",
      "caption": "The training-paradigm progression follows a decreasing-supervision gradient. Moving from distillation to SFT to RL to probing, the external supervision required falls monotonically and resistance to teacher-bias propagation rises, while direct optimization of the evaluation objective peaks at RL and drops at probing, which optimizes nothing but reads out what the frozen model already encodes. The three indices are ordinal encodings of the qualitative ranking argued in this appendix, not measured quantities.",
      "subcaption": null,
      "where": {
