      "caption": "Taxonomy of multi-agent evaluation strategies for SLM judges. Ensemble voting provides error decorrelation through independent cross-family panels. Multi-agent debate enables collective refinement but introduces sycophancy risks. Cascade routing optimizes cost through confidence-based escalation. Persona-based approaches increase evaluation diversity via role assignment. Section references indicate where each strategy is discussed in depth.",
